 198. Callee checksum rejection boundary: an imported-callee checksum mismatch rejects before child-workflow or child provider/command execution and performs no child-state identity remap, while ordinary parent-level metadata may already exist
 199. Cross-source identity boundary: equality of persisted step, checkpoint, call-frame, or other identities alone is not evidence that changed source can resume a supported old run
 200. Atomic upgrader ownership: any future supported cross-source transition is implemented and tested as one atomic upgrader that owns checksum and program-identity compatibility rather than as an evidence record, alias, or partial remap
+201. Resume projection audit ordering: after schema and root-checksum acceptance, `orchestrate resume` audits the root scope (module-level `audit_scope`) before observability overrides, executor-session/process metadata, executor construction, and the prologue; failure exits 1, prints the reason, and changes only the root `status`, `error`, and `updated_at`
+202. Structural-root executor guard: a root `WorkflowExecutor` rechecks the checksum through `StateManager.calculate_checksum` and then audits the root scope immediately before its prologue, persisting the `workflow_checksum_mismatch` envelope (reasons `workflow_modified`, `missing_recorded_checksum`, `missing_workflow_path`, `workflow_unavailable`) or the projection diagnostic with the same three-field delta; child call-frame executors do not repeat the guard
+203. Reached-call revalidation: a reached call performs one `resolve_call_boundary(slot_index, call_step_id)` lookup, selects the callee by the boundary's current alias, and revalidates frame shape, caller, alias, and lineage after input/checksum/bound-input validation but before the callee frame or state exists; nested scopes recurse
+204. Explicit identity fail-closed: stale, presentation-mismatched, out-of-scope, unclaimed, missing-required, and ambiguous explicit step/current/call identities fail with the twelve stable reasons; absent optional `step_id` rows stay compatible and are never backfilled
+205. Loop projection integrity: `for_each` and `repeat_until` bookkeeping violations (including the four admitted `repeat_until` forms) fail with `invalid_loop_progress` or `unsupported_shape`, and valid bookkeeping does not excuse a stale loop-local id
+206. Call-frame lineage: completed frames are unlimited history; non-Workflow-Lisp boundaries allow one non-completed frame; Workflow Lisp boundaries (typed `frontend_kind`) form one `::retry::<n>` lineage with predecessor-then-running validation order, deterministic lowest-unused retry allocation, and the `completed_call_frame_id_collision` rejection before any child exists
+207. Sticky projection failure: `resume_projection_integrity_error` is promoted unchanged through ancestor frames, is never consumed by routes, `on_error: continue`, or loop continuation, never wrapped in `call_failed`, and finalization failures are supplemental to it
+208. Forensic current step: an unchanged `current_step` left by a projection or checksum envelope is reported `pending`, not live, by status snapshots, markdown, heartbeat, and stalled-run interpretation
